# King Caradog (Caratacus): the long read (story-caradog.html), one timeline event, and the links to it.
# features.py adds STORY to the long reads; data.py adds EVENTS to the timeline.
# Asked for by Ifan, 12 November 2026: "Write a lot on Caratacus and Macsen Wledig", and yes to adding his life in Rome,
# the Claudia, Pudens and Linus of 2 Timothy 4:21, Martial's British Claudia Rufina, and Brân Fendigaid as his father.
# House rules (EDITORIAL.md): he is a king, never a chieftain; the people are Britons, never Celts; nothing negative about
# him; the Claudia/Linus/Brân traditions are told as "Welsh tradition holds", plainly and without a sneer.
# Quotations are only from named published translations:
#   Tacitus, Annals XII.34 and XII.37, tr. A. J. Church and W. J. Brodribb (1876), checked word for word, November 2026.
#   Dio Cassius LXI.33, tr. Earnest Cary (Loeb, 1924): "covet our poor tents".
#   2 Timothy 4:21 in the King James Version (1611) and in Y Beibl Cymraeg Newydd Diwygiedig (2004).
# Sources checked November 2026: Tacitus Annals XII.31-40; Dio LX.20-21, LXI.33; Martial Epigrams IV.13 and XI.53;
# Irenaeus, Against Heresies III.3.3; the Second Branch of the Mabinogi; Rachel Bromwich, Trioedd Ynys Prydein (triads 13, 95);
# Lady Charlotte Guest's notes to Branwen (1849) on the third-series triads (Myvyrian Archaiology, 1801);
# Theophilus Evans, Drych y Prif Oesoedd (1740 edition); Graham Webster, Rome against Caratacus (1981).
# Paragraph codes (see prose() in build.py): "## Heading", "> Quote | Source", "|| Left | Right".

