  sumEn="For nine years Caradog, son of King Cynfelyn, led the Britons of Wales against the legions of Rome. Taken in chains to Rome, he spoke before the emperor so boldly that he was set free. Welsh tradition holds that he was the son of Brân the Blessed, and that his children are named in the Bible.",
